Z||000000||JetroGT||11-17-1999||04:53 AM||||<BR>Thats right. The blue box under the passenger side dash. The problem is that it intermitently chimes for no reason. Is it just going bad? Cold solder maybe? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||11-17-1999||07:20 AM||||it should only chime when the door is open, keys in ignition, or your lights are on when car is off.....<P>if it is chiming otherwise...............pull it, it is not that valuable!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||11-17-1999||09:00 AM||||I'd say it could be coming from the parking brake switch.  Pop off the cover on the parking brake lever, there should be a pin and a contact, slightly bend the pin away, just a little.  This way the two shouldn't come in contact unless supposed to.  <BR>If you just want to turn off the parking brake chime completely(like I did): get under the dash on the passenger side.  Look up and coming out of the blue box will be a brown wire with a white stripe.  If you cut it, the parking brake chime will never go off again. But will still go off for lights,keys, etc. just not the parking brake.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-17-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||dogtired||11-17-1999||10:30 AM||||My vote is that it is going BAD? The one on my 86 seemed to have a mind of its own, would be going down the straight and level and it would go off, sometimes loud sometimes soft? I replaced it with one I got from this forum (Thanks Greg) and it works correctly. I do not like the anoying sound but I do like it working correctly. Keep those Blue Dingy Thingys moving around!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||Greg Piet||11-17-1999||07:18 PM||||I had and Olds Ciera, which one day just started beeping like a looney during a drive.  It met its doom under the front tire after that...   <BR>I think those dingy thingys just die all of a sudden,  I have replaced a few of them, after they went ballistic, and the replacements operate fine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||RZURCTN||11-17-1999||07:27 PM||||Or for all the latest on Blue Dingy info, you could do a search and come up with a 2 page thread on them! Very informative!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||11-17-1999||08:17 PM||||Indeed if you search for "Blue Ding Thingy", it'll find the thread!<P>Wonder if that phrase catches on in Fieroland.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||CUTTER||11-17-1999||10:10 PM||||Hey, my blue box thingy chimes too just when Im driving down the street. I was going to Harisburg PA from my house with my cousin (about 1 hour away) I been driving straight for about 30 mins and all of a sudden "ding, ding, ding" my cousin slowly turns his head and made a weird face and said "uhhh, let me guess...its supposed to do that?" and I said "yup, It does it all the time" It does it quiet offten, and everytime someone is driving with me when it does it they start laughing there @$$ off, because everyone always tells me how the fieros are "not wired right" and "its gonna catch fire and melt" everyone diss's my car....but when I race them....hmmm....the little "not wired right, fire hazard" beats them. Then im the one laughing. My car may chime when not supposed to, but your car is just plain slow!!!!!!   thats what I say.. Let the Fiero live!!!!!||||reg||1
